                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more weaselly"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "aeef21d1-70af-40cc-9dd7-aa97d071d8bf",
                        "entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "weasellier"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "56c59428-1753-477d-96f7-d0aecfbc4895",
                        "entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most weaselly"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "6ae62031-003d-41ad-ba0b-b102ff7f48bc",
                        "entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "weaselliest"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                        "entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling a weasel (in appearance)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76853e67-8d69-4ab3-a9b3-a9bd6585ab3c",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "The writer had just entered into his eighteenth year, when he met at the table of a certain Anglo-Germanist an individual, apparently somewhat under thirty, of middle stature, a thin and weaselly figure, a sallow complexion, a certain obliquity of vision, and a large pair of spectacles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68a7a9ee-07fc-4da1-9977-a9fa17f98b8b",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "“Pretty?”\n[…] Mr. Prestcott considered. “Fair to middling. Bit weaselly, if you know what I mean. Wouldn’t have been much without makeup. As it was, she managed to look quite attractive.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f67bcbe2-732d-4a7f-b663-9a64a9d70109",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "At three minutes past six the door opened to admit the naked, scrawny figure of Tingaling Bell. He had a sharp weasely face and a miserable body on which each bone showed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e223e7e-9f97-486e-a055-e597f539e4f7",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "On still weasellier, greasier members of the clique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0dcb3ce-3718-4f02-8a4b-4b8e9ba74336",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "I lifted the extension, slowly released the button, easing in mid-ring like the weaselliest weasel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6828b7a3-42f0-4ac6-90b9-ce2ba38c4f5f",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "He looks like a shorter, thinner, weasellier version of Tom Jones, and he sure knows how to work a crowd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "856782fd-5835-4eb3-a498-2497f2fb48f4",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "That was when the constantly complaining but unseen dog showed itself, if it was actually a dog. The weaselly little creature crawled out from under the couch—more rodential than canine, Pepe thought."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "face3470-39fb-4dbe-9631-c891b93c89d0",
                                "sense_id": "bf593387-4840-3e5d-8569-33840dd51e60",
                                "text": "More members arrive. […] Lucifer, small and fat and weasellier (e.g. more like a weasel) than ever, and a few other nonentities whose names Fricka can never remember."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                        "entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Devious; cunning; misleading; sneaky."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae606c04-ad22-4585-b1a2-f7cca6bf4f00",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "1864, W. S. Gilbert, “Sixty-Three and Sixty-Four” originally published in Fun, V (2 January 1864), p. 162, later published in Bab Ballads, Cambridge, Massachusetts: Belknap Press of Harvard University Press, 1970, p. 37,\nWith intellect weaselly, artist has easily earned all his bacon and greens by it,\nAnd now that it’s done and all ready for Fun, it’s my duty to say what he means by it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "289d6380-199e-4a6a-9d4c-2f1e02f1645d",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "“Ah was vara weaselly. Ah wasna going home without yon stoof for Captain Harker. Vara coonning ah was.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d7f5f48-ca26-45c4-b955-8e11de4a39ec",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "Menemencioglu could see no good reason why this weasely document should not be interpreted so as to keep Turkey out of a war in which he and the other Turkish leaders were convinced she could do no better than be uselessly crushed […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7682360f-2a55-473b-97f3-e88792a38858",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "“There’s a poem I like,” Harry said. “By Robert Graves. About cats. Cats, he says, make their point by walking round it. It’s all right for cats. For humans, as you say—weaselly. Why don’t they come out with it?”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56bad49f-57b3-42f0-8485-6e8adcbe0fdc",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "It was one of the strangest elections I have ever witnessed, even odder than the 1988 presidential race, when two yahoos named George Bush and Michael Dukakis ended what Hunter S. Thompson declared “The Generation of Swine” by conducting the weaselliest, most vacuous, idealess campaign in the nation’s history."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f203ab2d-8a7c-402f-99a1-5bc6d1175d4b",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "Charles Lucas received the most weaselly rejection, the directors hoping they might be able to programme his symphony, but adding that they ‘would by no means wish to prevent his so doing elsewhere’."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09fc2364-16e2-4f7c-bd80-077f679f88f1",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "“Rat-faced. Never trust a reporter. They’re weasellier than rodents!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b1c055c-d8c1-4fb2-b623-4aacc6987977",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "So gas rustlers are the horse thieves of the 21st century. The weaselliest are the pump-and-run variety. They strike even in broad daylight. They fill ’er up, then skedaddle without paying."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f87355d2-f450-4c82-8779-51df6d60dcb4",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "There’s a weaselly feel to the plan, a sense that tough decisions were postponed even as President Obama warns about our “perfect storm of financial problems.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f31c80f-d355-4096-93bf-67909a066441",
                                "sense_id": "e4e85770-38ef-3b21-97f9-1c37e824c8d0",
                                "text": "If the prompting is necessary, email (or text) is arguably the worst, weaselliest possible way to do it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "870a3a31-1eb3-4360-b623-779b709b198c",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "source_sense_description": "devious, cunning, sneaky",
                        "target_lang_word": "sournois",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sournois",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "687bd130-dfe1-395d-8253-39715ec76b4e",
                                        "entry_id": "883722c6-0c40-3ea8-9251-1bb30411d61c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui cache ce qu’il pense dans un but malveillant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "110ffe4c-4b7f-4be1-9a7b-9a289d8f1812",
                                                "sense_id": "687bd130-dfe1-395d-8253-39715ec76b4e",
                                                "text": "Les petits voleurs restaient, les uns debout, les autres accotés contre le lit ou la huche, tous morveux et sales, bien portants d’ailleurs, grugeant leurs prunes sans rien dire, mais regardant l’étranger d’un œil sournois et narquois."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc749584-dfcb-47e0-9512-0f957a2b7707",
                                                "sense_id": "687bd130-dfe1-395d-8253-39715ec76b4e",
                                                "text": "Deux hommes sortirent de la cabine. Ils étaient gras et luisants, avec un air de prospérité sournoise sur toute leur personne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5019f3ac-ebe4-4675-b672-28c3451ed5f5",
                                                "sense_id": "687bd130-dfe1-395d-8253-39715ec76b4e",
                                                "text": "Et chacun de me plaisanter ; ma jeunesse à son lever, mon parfum de fille fraîche, ma chair toute neuve en son premier éclat éveillaient chez les hommes de sournoises concupiscences, aiguisaient leur regard."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a518190-5920-3e24-80f6-fe950f8a23a7",
                                        "entry_id": "883722c6-0c40-3ea8-9251-1bb30411d61c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui ne se manifeste pas clairement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d55d4e63-7f18-42d8-8987-8bde97b8c173",
                                                "sense_id": "5a518190-5920-3e24-80f6-fe950f8a23a7",
                                                "text": "Énorme oiseau de proie, mon avion, désormais hélas ! en pleine lumière, décrit lentement des orbes sournois."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe1ba7e5-8e9d-4503-abea-1b5bf62acd4b",
                                                "sense_id": "5a518190-5920-3e24-80f6-fe950f8a23a7",
                                                "text": "C’était un « melon » qui naturellement, subissait toutes les phases du cabossage et de l’aplatissement. Son possesseur avait beau le retaper, l’épousseter, le placer à distance, une fatalité sournoise voulait que, tout à coup, tantôt l’un, tantôt l’autre des acrobates s’élançât à pieds joints sur lui."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d4969f4-7120-4c47-9ce6-7a1e570632a0",
                                                "sense_id": "5a518190-5920-3e24-80f6-fe950f8a23a7",
                                                "text": "Le cancer est une maladie sournoise, d’où l’importance des campagnes de dépistage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7be2817b-d0bd-419d-a127-1076d5b16af1",
                                                "sense_id": "5a518190-5920-3e24-80f6-fe950f8a23a7",
                                                "text": "Surtout, 2021 nous révélera ses répercussions les plus sournoises, celles qui perdureront pendant des années."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sournois",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "003a8078-097e-3d54-95af-353ac98e9eab",
                                        "entry_id": "da9525bb-906e-3660-ae21-7c5205983dcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne sournoise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21018cca-26be-46a8-a44c-b6ffb35c2061",
                                                "sense_id": "003a8078-097e-3d54-95af-353ac98e9eab",
                                                "text": "Le drôle voyait bien. Une femme jolie, fraîche, tendre, mécontente d’un mari volage, peu connue, et qui ne faisait point d’enfants ; Sylvina, enfin, au point où le sournois se proposait de l’amener, le friand morceau pour un saint homme !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3dc56bf-9968-4cb0-aa58-3ca1aeaa693b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e6c0a657-abb2-3ff3-a2e0-db5bf11e8b58",
                        "source_sense_description": "devious, cunning, sneaky",
                        "target_lang_word": "verschlagen",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verschlagen",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4233172-dbd5-37e9-9e3a-e5560da31a79",
                                        "entry_id": "2d99d2ed-c141-31cf-9049-9f62114305d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "auf geschickte und verdeckte Art und Weise eigennützig"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5071482-5365-41a2-9030-1edb95c942fd",
                                                "sense_id": "c4233172-dbd5-37e9-9e3a-e5560da31a79",
                                                "text": "Er war schon immer ein verschlagener Bursche."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abb53676-3b01-4003-ad99-ea011a467f53",
                                                "sense_id": "c4233172-dbd5-37e9-9e3a-e5560da31a79",
                                                "text": "„Nicht anonyme Mächte – Menschen machen Geschichte. Es hängt entscheidend viel davon ab, ob die politisch Verantwortlichen aufrichtig oder verschlagen miteinander umgehen, ob sie es darauf anlegen, ihr Gegenüber zu vernichten, oder ob sie auf nachhaltige Partnerschaft aus sind.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "faf46ef0-269f-370b-8f78-4b413d2b6e50",
                                        "entry_id": "2d99d2ed-c141-31cf-9049-9f62114305d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "geringfügig angewärmt, bei Wasser zum Beispiel weniger als handwarm, sogar weniger als lauwarm"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7a44bf7-aefe-45c8-a0f8-9c866a7a9844",
                                                "sense_id": "faf46ef0-269f-370b-8f78-4b413d2b6e50",
                                                "text": "„Auch in einigen Ställen Deutschlands ist es gebräuchlich geworden, die Pferde nach jedem Dienste mit verschlagenem Wasser zu waschen, sie danach gut abzutrocknen und einzudecken.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "verschlagen",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "151efeb7-88a9-3c43-bcdb-fe0e24e1df93",
                                        "entry_id": "467bb7dd-0f5a-3f55-a45e-8d862aa040f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "versehentlich die aktuell beachtete Seite eines Buches zuschlagen und eine andere aufschlagen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1afabd7b-be24-4a95-99ef-fb56f0da9dac",
                                                "sense_id": "151efeb7-88a9-3c43-bcdb-fe0e24e1df93",
                                                "text": "Au, jetzt habe ich die Seite verschlagen."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6c0e045-4ee1-3bcf-82bb-a35c878b9835",
                                        "entry_id": "467bb7dd-0f5a-3f55-a45e-8d862aa040f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "an eine Stelle geraten, an die man ursprünglich nicht hinkommen wollte"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb9bd427-70f5-4cc9-b841-5bcb19bde244",
                                                "sense_id": "c6c0e045-4ee1-3bcf-82bb-a35c878b9835",
                                                "text": "Viele Deutsche hat es im letzten Weltkrieg nach Übersee verschlagen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e14ca40e-f84c-48e7-9aaa-c09176f10a4c",
                                                "sense_id": "c6c0e045-4ee1-3bcf-82bb-a35c878b9835",
                                                "text": "Wie hat es denn dich hierhin verschlagen?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a39ce62-fb1a-4acf-a2d3-c891eccb79e4",
                                                "sense_id": "c6c0e045-4ee1-3bcf-82bb-a35c878b9835",
                                                "text": "„Zum Radio hat es mich verschlagen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "606bcfaa-fd6d-3dcf-8cd3-e3be584c4b26",
                                        "entry_id": "467bb7dd-0f5a-3f55-a45e-8d862aa040f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "jemandem mit Schlägen körperliche Schmerzen zufügen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "regional"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af6a52bb-197e-49f1-b14f-61b24dd61886",
                                                "sense_id": "606bcfaa-fd6d-3dcf-8cd3-e3be584c4b26",
                                                "text": "Lass uns ihn verschlagen gehen."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b0fcb80d-8a64-3b28-bf2d-82a87ae235aa",
                                        "entry_id": "467bb7dd-0f5a-3f55-a45e-8d862aa040f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "abrupt dafür sorgen, dass etwas nicht mehr ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "jemandem etwas verschlagen"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b413c17-368b-4245-8220-63e721d5c366",
                                                "sense_id": "b0fcb80d-8a64-3b28-bf2d-82a87ae235aa",
                                                "text": "Es verschlägt mir die Sprache!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a991d8d-e986-498d-b343-600a1b6c36ca",
                                                "sense_id": "b0fcb80d-8a64-3b28-bf2d-82a87ae235aa",
                                                "text": "Der Geruch verschlug ihnen den Appetit."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"4\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdfec9d3-e125-3e30-8d38-4f06a029e8b2",
                                        "entry_id": "467bb7dd-0f5a-3f55-a45e-8d862aa040f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "einen Ball so treffen, dass er nicht dort landet, wo geplant"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d5c7ace-b3ee-4687-b8a7-83059733f0d5",
                                                "sense_id": "bdfec9d3-e125-3e30-8d38-4f06a029e8b2",
                                                "text": "Sie verschlägt den Ball, der knapp im Aus landet."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"5\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c21142f-f887-3fcd-a7f2-005344a8cdb4",
                                        "entry_id": "467bb7dd-0f5a-3f55-a45e-8d862aa040f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine flüssige Masse mit einer Gabel oder einem Schneebesen mit etwas anderem vermischen"
                                        ],
